public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination.ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels.Catalogue
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination.ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels.LocalSections
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination.ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels.CubicControl

/-!
# Binary component reduction for 15.3.49(l)

The shared target list uses concrete group equivalences. The local section
lemmas identify the intrinsic component quotient with its star image and
justify the literal Sylow intersection. The cubic-control argument excludes
an invariant solvable envelope generated by cubic elements whose order is
divisible by nine, using universal (j) and θ(M ∩ H) = Y₀.

The source assembly still needs the binary model sieve from the precise
appendix alternatives, construction of the cubic envelope in the nontrivial
L₃(2) orbit, and the subgroup geometry identifying Y₀*T₀* as the indicated
minimal parabolic. None of these is supplied by the shared target definition.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed
pp.1143–1144, especially clause (l).
-/

@[expose] public section

open Subgroup
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination.ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels

/-- An intrinsic classification of L/O₂(L) identifies the actual star image. -/
theorem starImage_model {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G]
    (H L : Subgroup G) (hLH : L ≤ H) (hL : (L.subgroupOf H).IsCComponent)
    (hm : BinaryComponentModel (L ⧸ pCore 2 L)) : BinaryComponentModel (starImage H L) :=
  hm.of_mulEquiv (componentStarEquiv H L hLH hL).symm

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination.ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels
